error[E0105]: expected `do` after `quote`, found `{`
  --> tests/ui/ruby_habits.wid:11:9
   |
11 |   quote { 1 }
   |         ^ a `quote` takes its code in `do … end`, not in braces
   = note: `quote` is a keyword, not a method that takes a block
help: write `do … end`
   |   quote do 1 end
   = see `wid explain E0105`

error[E0105]: expected `def` after `macro`, found `twice`
  --> tests/ui/ruby_habits.wid:15:7
   |
15 | macro twice(e: Code) -> Code
   |       ^^^^^ expected `def`
   | ----- a macro is declared with `macro def`
help: add `def`
   | macro def twice(e: Code) -> Code
   = see `wid explain E0105`

error[E0301]: expected `Code`, found `String`
  --> tests/ui/ruby_habits.wid:23:3
   |
23 |   "#{e} * 3"
   |   ^^^^^^^^^^ this has type `String`
help: a macro builds code with `quote do … end`, not with a string; in a `quote`, `#{…}` splices a value in
   |   quote do
   |     #{e} * 3
   |   end
   = see `wid explain E0301`

error[E0105]: a `guard`'s `else` branch goes on the lines below it
  --> tests/ui/ruby_habits.wid:46:20
   |
46 |   guard x = v else return 0
   |                    ^^^^^^^^ this branch is on the `guard`'s line
   = note: the branch is a block: it starts on the next line, leaves the scope and ends with `end`
help: put the branch on its own line, and close it with `end`
   |   guard x = v else
   |     return 0
   |   end
   = see `wid explain E0105`

error[E0319]: the macro `timed` does not take a block
  --> tests/ui/ruby_habits.wid:52:9
   |
52 |   timed do
   |         ^^ this block is never used
help: pass the code as an argument instead; a `Code` parameter receives it unevaluated
